  "narrative": [
    "All departmental courses taken to satisfy the requirements of the literature major, including courses in the secondary literature, must be taken for a letter grade. No grade below C- is acceptable for a course taken in the major.",
    "At least six of the upper-division courses for the major, including a minimum of four in the primary literature, must be taken at UC San Diego.",
    "Special studies courses (198s and 199s) may not be used to satisfy upper-division requirements for majors or minors.",
    "Students who take Education Abroad Program or Opportunities Abroad Program (EAP/OAP) courses in a country appropriate to their major may use up to five upper-division courses to satisfy major requirements.",
    "Intensive Track Option (optional, noted on transcript): in addition to the secondary language requirements, students in the intensive track will complete at least two upper-division literature courses taught in the language used to fulfill their secondary language requirement."
